## 4. Phase 2 — the responsive foundation

### 4.1 One token layer

New `client/src/styles/mobile-tokens.css`, applied at the phone app root:

> **Corrected 2026-08-17 after review.** The first draft of this block used
> `--u: clamp(0.84, calc(100cqi / 390), 1.10)` as a unitless ratio. That is invalid CSS —
> `100cqi / 390` is a *length*, and `clamp()` cannot mix a length with unitless numbers.
> Verified in the repo's Chromium 125: every declaration consuming it falls back, so
> `padding-left: calc(4px * var(--u))` computes to **`0px`**. CSS cannot divide a length by
> a length, so a viewport-derived unitless ratio is not expressible at all. Tokens are
> therefore **length-valued**, each with its own clamp.

```css
.tp-viewport {
  container-type: inline-size;          /* size off our own 430px-capped box, not the window */

  /* Each token is a length with its own clamp. The middle term is calibrated so the
     390px reference viewport reproduces today's design value exactly; the floor holds
     at 320 and the ceiling stops growth past 430. Verified: 4.1cqi at a 390 container
     = 15.99px. */
  --sp-1: clamp( 3px, 1.03cqi,  4.4px);
  --sp-2: clamp( 7px, 2.05cqi,  8.8px);
  --sp-3: clamp(10px, 3.08cqi, 13.2px);
  --sp-4: clamp(13px, 4.10cqi, 17.6px);
  --sp-6: clamp(20px, 6.15cqi, 26.4px);
  --sp-7: clamp(23px, 7.18cqi, 30.8px);

  --bar-h: clamp(32px,  9.74cqi, 41.8px);   /* the action bar's *only* height source */
  --row-h: clamp(54px, 16.41cqi, 70.4px);   /* one active-stack row */

  --safe-top:    env(safe-area-inset-top, 0px);
  --safe-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom, 0px);
  --safe-left:   env(safe-area-inset-left, 0px);    /* landscape — see §4.3 */
  --safe-right:  env(safe-area-inset-right, 0px);

  height: 100vh;      /* fallback order matters */
  height: 100svh;
  height: 100dvh;
}
```

If a single driving ratio ever proves necessary, the only legal form is an
`@property { syntax: "<number>" }` custom property written from JS by a `ResizeObserver` —
verified working (`calc(4px * var(--r) * 4)` → 14.4px at `--r: 0.9`). Do not reach for it
first; per-token clamps need no JS and no registration.

**Gate this, don't trust it.** A computed-style test is mandatory for every token: render
`.tp-viewport` at 320 / 390 / 430 and assert each token's `getComputedStyle` value is a
non-zero length within tolerance of the intended number. The failure mode above is silent
— nothing errors, everything just becomes `0px`.

Container queries (`cqi`, `container-type`) are Baseline since Safari 16 / Chrome 105 and
need no build support — Vite 5 + Tailwind 3.4 pass them through untouched. Using `cqi`
rather than `vw` is what makes the same components correct inside the landing page's
phone demo and on a tablet, not only in a full-window phone.

### 4.2 Rules that replace the current habits

| Instead of | Use |
|---|---|
| `fontSize: 88` | `font-size: clamp(<floor>, <fluid cqi>, <ceiling>)` from the type ramp |
| `padding: '154px 22px 90px'` | grid rows + measured gutters (§5.2) |
| `height: '50%'` | `grid-template-rows` with `minmax()` |
| `height: 100vh` | the `svh`/`dvh` chain above |
| hardcoded notch/home-indicator clearance | `var(--safe-top)` / `var(--safe-bottom)` |
| a hardcoded `height` on any flex child | a token, and `min-height: 0` on the scroll parent |

Every fixed dimension gets a `clamp()` whose floor still works at **320×568** (per D2).

